{"answer":"Not a bug — it's the recorded behavior. `init()` explicitly checks `if (fs.existsSync(tomlPath) && !force)`, logs `small.toml already exists — use --force to overwrite`, and returns `true` without touching the file (packages/cli/lib/init.js:12-15). The SKILL.md doc confirms this is deliberate: "It never overwrites an existing `small.toml` (`--force` to regenerate)" (skills/small/SKILL.md:18-19). So the design intent is to protect any manual edits you've made to small.toml (e.g. filled-in secrets or entry) from being silently clobbered by a re-scan.

To deliberately regenerate it, pass the force flag: `small init --force`. That flows through `bin/small.js`'s `init` command (`init(process.cwd(), { force: !!flags.force })`, packages/cli/bin/small.js:51) into `init.js`, which then re-detects the entry/framework/secrets and rewrites the file from scratch.

No reason beyond "protect existing file" is recorded in these sources — if you want confirmation of the exact rationale (e.g. whether it should merge rather than fully overwrite on --force), that's not captured here and would need to be asked of the builder.","citations":[{"kind":"code","path":"packages/cli/lib/init.js","start_line":10,"end_line":15},{"kind":"code","path":"skills/small/SKILL.md","start_line":16,"end_line":19},{"kind":"code","path":"packages/cli/bin/small.js","start_line":50,"end_line":52}]}
